    <h2>Where I am now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Education:</strong> B.S. in Information Technology, specializing in Information Assurance and Cybersecurity (Capella University, 2026)</li>
      <li><strong>Certification:</strong> Practical OSINT Research Professional (PORP), TCM Security</li>
      <li><strong>Internship:</strong> Interning with <em>The OSINT Insider</em> under Managing Editor Rachel Brooks since September 2026 — working where OSINT meets journalism</li>
      <li><strong>Volunteering:</strong> Onboarding with the Skull Games Task Force, an OSINT-for-good volunteer group that assists law enforcement against predators and traffickers</li>
      <li><strong>Practice:</strong> Trace Labs Search Party CTF competitor and KaseScenarios practitioner</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What is OSINT?</h2>
    <p>Open source intelligence is the process of collecting and analyzing information from publicly available sources. That includes social media, public records, news articles, websites, maps, images, and anything else accessible without specialized access or illegal methods.</p>
    <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Book and course reviews on OSINT, investigations, and counter-trafficking</li>
      <li>Reflections on certifications, CTFs, and hands-on practice</li>
      <li>Notes on ethics, privacy, and operational security</li>
      <li>Milestones on the road toward mission-driven analyst work</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The through-line: learning to do online research well, and aiming it at the people who need it most.</p>
